  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be a non-constant polynomial such that <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> Then the minimum number of roots of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> in <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is/are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0097_596ecc441106.png\" style=\"width:2.35347in;height:1.38681in\" /><br />As <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then by Rolle’s theorem, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> <math><mo>⇒</mo></math> for some <math><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Again, applying Rolle’s theorem to function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math></p><p>we have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence, the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has at least one root.</p>"
  }
